4.3 Energy and TCO

Monthly consumption is computed from measured average draw at the wall, not TDP sums:

E = P_{\text{avg measured}} \times h \times 30

At 0.8 kW average over 8 h/day, ~192 kWh/month. At 1.2 kW continuous, ~864 kWh/month. The monetary cost depends on the applicable tariff and is included in the 12–36 month TCO alongside room cooling and the recurring API budget.

Buy-versus-API rule. The purchase is justified only if the measured local cost per successful task beats the API cost per successful task for the same reference workload over a 24-month horizon:

\text{Local cost per task} = \frac{\text{amortised hardware} + \text{energy} + \text{cooling}}{\text{successful tasks per month}}

\text{API cost per task} = \text{measured API spend} \div \text{successful tasks}

Self-hosted break-even against frontier APIs ranges from ~5M to ~250M tokens per month depending on what is counted, and prompt caching can cut realised API cost by ~88% on cache-heavy agent workloads. The benchmark must produce this number, not assume it.

