5. Benchmark protocol

The benchmark is executed on rented GPU capacity before any purchase. A week of rental on a 5090-class instance costs a small fraction of the price of a wrong purchase.

5.1 Workload and concurrency

The 40/30/20/10 reference mix, with real SI TEAM tasks. Concurrency 5, 10, 20, and 40 simultaneous logical agents. Active inference requests are recorded separately from agent count. Context 4K, 8K, 32K; a 128K sub-test for the DGX Spark only. Duration: 1 h validation, 8 h sustained, 24 h acceptance.

5.2 Model classes — dense, MoE, hybrid

Class Candidate Why it is tested
Dense Qwen3-32B at 4-bit Baseline for interactive latency; full-attention KV formula applies
Sparse MoE GPT-OSS-120B (117B total, 5.1B active) Tests whether active-parameter decoding meets interactive thresholds on one GPU
Hybrid / long-context A hybrid-attention 27B–35B class model Tests whether a non-standard KV layout changes the capacity calculus; software maturity on sm_120 is a risk to measure

The benchmark records decode tok/s, prefill tok/s, TTFT p95, TPOT p95, and quality on the SI TEAM critical-analysis task for each class.

5.3 Engine comparison

vLLM and SGLang on the same hardware, same model, same workload, 20 agents. Record TTFT p50/p95/p99, TPOT p95, preemption rate, KV pool size, and task success. Apply the selection rule of §3.5.

5.4 KV quality tests

FP16/BF16 vs FP8 needle-in-a-haystack at 4K and 32K on sm_120, using SI TEAM tasks, not synthetic prompts. FP8 is accepted for the generalist engine only if accuracy is within 2 percentage points of BF16 and the reasoning test is not degraded. The critic engine remains BF16 until it passes the same test under FP8.

5.5 Power-cap measurement

Dual 5090 at 575 W vs 450 W, same workload. Record decode tok/s, TTFT p95, TPOT p95, and wall power. The 450 W cap is adopted if the throughput loss is ≤ 15%. If the loss is > 25%, dual-5090 Mode B is rejected.

5.6 Day-in-the-life test

One working day of the actual SI TEAM workload: twenty agents, real documents, real API fallback. Record task completion time, agent idle time, queue wait time, human intervention rate, and cost per successful task. A configuration that meets p95 TPOT but leaves agents waiting in the queue for minutes has failed the orchestration requirement, not the inference requirement.

5.7 Acceptance thresholds

Metric Threshold Action if failed
Platform burn-in 72 h without crash, PCIe loss, or memory error Do not proceed; diagnose platform
p95 TPOT (interactive) ≤ 100 ms Reduce batch or context; requalify
p95 TTFT (interactive) ≤ 2 s Reduce queue depth; enable chunked prefill
24 h, 20 agents ≥ 99% task success, excluding external API errors Investigate; do not purchase until corrected
Memory No fatal OOM during 24 h Adjust context, KV precision, or batch ceiling
Preemption rate Recorded; no unbounded growth under load Tighten batch ceiling or KV budget
Thermal GPU < 83 °C, throttle < 5% Redesign cooling before purchase
Power (Mode B) No shutdown, no trip; 450 W cap loss ≤ 15% Upgrade PSU or reject dual-5090 Mode B
TCO Measured local cost/task ≤ API cost/task over 24 months Do not purchase

5.8 Tooling and reproducibility

A measurement harness injects the 20-agent workload and logs TTFT, TPOT, tokens/s, KV pool size, preemption rate, and cost per task. Image versions are pinned (vLLM, SGLang, CUDA, driver). cache_salt is set per request and verified present in logs. Without this harness the benchmark cannot be reproduced and the purchase cannot be justified.

