Appendix B — Memory subsystem and population rules

The Threadripper PRO 9965WX exposes an 8-channel DDR5 memory interface, one DIMM per channel, with a maximum of 8 RDIMMs per processor. Populating fewer than eight channels degrades aggregate bandwidth proportionally; populating more than one DIMM per channel is not supported on WRX90.

Population Capacity with 16 GB modules Capacity with 32 GB modules Bandwidth efficiency
4 DIMMs (one per channel pair) 64 GB 128 GB ~50–60% of peak
8 DIMMs (one per channel) 128 GB 256 GB ~100% of peak

The staged build populates 8×16 GB RDIMM at 5600 MT/s, delivering 128 GB across all eight channels. This satisfies the dual requirement of full channel population and bounded capital outlay. The board supports speeds up to 6400 MT/s with validated RDIMM kits; running at 5600 MT/s is a stability margin, not a platform limit.

Memory capacity is not the binding constraint for the orchestrator. The binding constraint is VRAM. The 128 GB stage covers PostgreSQL, Prometheus, the corpus cache, the result registry, and twenty agent-state records with headroom; expansion to 256 GB follows only if measurement shows system RAM utilisation above 80% during the 24-hour acceptance run.

