Appendix H — Storage and data residency architecture

Data class Residence Sensitivity Protection Restore test
Model weights ZFS mirror, 2× 4 TB PCIe 5.0 NVMe Public Re-download or reinstall Not required (public artefact)
Active KV cache GPU VRAM Ephemeral None Not applicable
Agent state RAM + PostgreSQL on data NVMe Internal Encrypted at rest; daily snapshot Monthly
Corpus Data NVMe (4 TB) + 10 GbE NAS Variable ZFS snapshots; versioning Monthly
Execution logs Data NVMe + Prometheus Internal (no raw prompts) Encrypted at rest; task IDs, metrics, fingerprints only Monthly
API keys HashiCorp Vault or equivalent Critical Encrypted, offline backup Quarterly
Results and provenance Research repository Internal Versioned; monthly restore test Monthly

The ZFS mirror uses two identical PCIe 5.0 NVMe drives with DRAM cache. DRAM-less drives are excluded from the system mirror because their write amplification and latency variance under sustained checkpointing are unacceptable for a PostgreSQL journal and model-weight volume. The data volume is a separate 4 TB NVMe drive plus the 10 GbE NAS; separating system and data volumes allows the system mirror to be rebuilt without touching the corpus.

Execution logs must not contain complete user prompts. Log entries carry the task identifier, model version, execution parameters, TTFT, TPOT, token count, and a content fingerprint (SHA-256 of the prompt), but not the prompt text. The fingerprint supports reproducibility and provenance without creating a second copy of confidential content.

