Appendix J — Benchmark execution sequence

The benchmark is executed in strict order. A failure at any stage stops the sequence; later stages are not run on a failed platform.

Stage Duration Pass criterion If fail
1. Platform burn-in 72 h Appendix D thermal + AER + memory + ZFS scrub Diagnose platform; do not proceed
2. Single-GPU baseline 8 h 32B dense at 32K, batch 1–4, no OOM Reduce context or KV precision; requalify
3. KV quality 4 h FP8 within 2 pp of BF16 on SI TEAM reasoning task Critic engine stays BF16; generalist may still use FP8 if retrieval passes
4. Engine comparison 8 h vLLM vs SGLang TTFT p95 at 20 agents Apply Appendix F.3 rule
5. MoE track 8 h GPT-OSS-120B decode ≥ 30 tok/s at batch 1 MoE is batch-only; dense 32B remains interactive engine
6. Power-cap test 4 h 450 W inference loss ≤ 15% vs 575 W Reject dual-5090 Mode B if > 25%; 15–25% is conditional
7. Day-in-the-life 8 h (one working day) Task completion, queue wait, human intervention recorded If queue wait dominates, the architecture fails the orchestration requirement
8. TCO computation 1 h Local cost/task ≤ API cost/task over 24 months Do not purchase; remain on API

Stage 1 is the gate. A node that passes stages 2–8 but fails stage 1 is not a reliable orchestration node, and its inference numbers are not evidence for a purchase.

